WEBVTT

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.580
Faster!  It’ll catch us!

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.830
I never thought I'd battle Revolver here.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:29.980
But to let people know what’s 
happening, I must win!

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.720
I run Across the universe

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.890
At the speed of light

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:54.760
Begin Loading

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.500
Open the door of dreams

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.070
VRAINS spreads

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.170
Believe in myself

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.710
VRAINS continues

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:14.020
The circuit draws the future

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:18.090
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.690
Access!

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.390
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:23.990
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.290
Link with my soul

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.060
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:30.800
Now Win the Race

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.640
Connected world

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.140
No matter when

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:40.510
Nothing is impossible

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:44.650
Strive for hope

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.230
And ride the wind!

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.450
Here I go.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.910
My turn.  I draw!

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:13.480
I summon Gateway Dragon from my hand.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.340
Gateway Dragon’s effect.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:25.300
I Special Summon a Level 4 or 
lower Dark Dragon from my hand.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.790
I call forth Sniffer Dragon!

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:38.900
Due to Sniffer Dragon’s effect, I add 
another Sniffer Dragon from my deck to my hand.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:43.380
As I’ve seen before, you don’t use an AI.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.660
Trusting an AI is foolish.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.770
You said the Ignis would destroy the world.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.060
What do you mean?

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.990
A moneygrubber like you can’t understand.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:59.460
His deck's ace is a powerful, 
high Link monster.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:06.830
The longer this duel lasts, the 
more I’m at a disadvantage.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:11.540
I discard Level 5 Background Dragon...

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.080
...to Special Summon Defrag 
Dragon from my hand!

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:25.280
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:31.760
The summoning conditions are two 
Level 4 or lower non-Token Dragons!

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.500
I set Gateway Dragon and Sniffer Dragon!

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.400
Link Summon!

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.160
Appear, Link 2 Twin Triangle Dragon!

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.420
Twin Triangle...

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.500
He has a Level 5 monster in his graveyard!

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.950
Twin Triangle Dragon’s effect activates.

00:03:57.950 --> 00:04:00.420
I pay 500 LP.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:06.530
I Special Summon a Level 5 or higher monster 
from my graveyard next to its link.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:09.500
Resurrect, Background Dragon!

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:18.480
The Special Summoned monster loses 
its effects and can’t attack.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.640
He wants to end this duel quick!

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:24.340
He's summoning a Link 4 monster!

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:28.650
Manifest!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.400
Arrowheads confirmed.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.900
The summoning conditions 
are at least two monsters.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:45.750
I set Defrag Dragon, Background Dragon and 
Link 2 Twin Triangle Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:53.740
Link Summon!

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:58.380
Appear, Link 4 Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:06.730
He easily summoned a Link 4 monster!

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:09.730
I set one card.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.360
Besides battle damage, Topologic 
Bomber Dragon deals damage...

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:19.240
...equal to the ATK of the 
monster it's attacking.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:24.410
And its effect destroys everything 
in the Main Monster Zone.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:28.000
Unless I stop Topologic, I can’t win.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.280
I must seal away its effects!

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:34.150
Go, Topologic Bomber Dragon!

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.250
Attack Marionetter!

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:40.260
Ultimate Malicious Code!

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:47.540
When your monster attacks, if I 
have an Altergeist on my field...

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:53.670
...I can Special Summon Altergeist Kunquery 
from my hand and negate that attack!

00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:01.340
And as long as I have Kunquery, 
Topologic’s effects are negated!

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:06.320
I survived his ace’s attack 
and sealed away its effects.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.920
I end my turn.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:16.760
Just as Playmaker said, something 
is happening in LINK VRAINS.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:21.640
What are you going to 
use all this energy for?

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:27.100
Something unimaginable will happen soon.

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:30.970
Hanoi are planning something terrifying.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:36.060
I came for a treasure hunt, but 
I didn’t expect to find this.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.440
I need to take this data out of here.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:40.730
I must win somehow!

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.940
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:46.850
I summon Altergeist Silquitous!

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:53.460
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Altergeist Protocol!

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.450
Next up, Silquitous’s effect!

00:06:56.450 --> 00:07:03.820
An Altergeist on my field and a card 
on your field return to our hands!

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:06.050
I return Protocol to my hand.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:07.280
Revolver!

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.740
I return Topologic Bomber 
Dragon to your hand!

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.760
A Link Monster doesn’t return to the hand.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.220
Therefore…

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:18.420
It returns to the Extra Deck.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:24.130
I completely sealed away 
Topologic Bomber Dragon.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:26.490
Now I can make my move!

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.330
Open before me!

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:32.460
The circuit that connects to 
the unknown parallel universe!

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:37.070
The summoning conditions are two Altergeists.

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:40.470
I set Kunquery and Silquitous!

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:43.810
Link Summon!

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:49.020
Appear, Link 2 Altergeist Kidolga!

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.800
Open again!

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.460
The circuit that connects to 
the unknown parallel universe!

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.300
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.870
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Altergeists!

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:11.310
I set Marionetter and Link 2 
Kidolga in the Link Markers!

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:14.440
Circuit combine!

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.450
Link Summon!

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:22.450
Appear, Link 3 Altergeist Primebanshee!

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:30.660
I activate the trap card, 
Altergeist Manifestation!

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:35.760
I Special Summon one Altergeist from my 
graveyard and equip it with this card!

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:38.560
What I need isn’t attack strength.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:41.000
I need an effect to 
capitalize on this chance.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:45.740
I resurrect Altergeist Kidolga!

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:51.240
I set two cards!

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:56.280
You chose a monster that 
doesn’t rely on ATK?

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:59.160
You’ll find out why soon enough.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:02.160
He has a set card on his field.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:06.500
But if I don’t make my move now, 
I won’t get a second chance.

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.400
I’m going for it!

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:13.230
Battle!  Altergeist Primebanshee 
attacks you directly!

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.950
Venom Duct!

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.680
It's working!

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:30.020
His set card can't stop attacks!

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:33.010
Next, Kidolga’s effect.

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:37.490
When another Altergeist 
deals you battle damage...

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:42.870
...I can Special Summon a Link Monster 
from your graveyard next to its link.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:47.640
I Special Summon Twin Triangle 
Dragon from Revolver’s graveyard!

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:50.670
This is why you chose Kidolga.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.700
It's now over.

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:00.990
First, Altergeist Kidolga 
attacks Revolver directly!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.590
Trespasser Edge!

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:08.790
The opponent has 400 LP left.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.450
That's what you get for mocking me.

00:10:11.450 --> 00:10:14.100
I’ll defeat you with your own monster!

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:18.330
Twin Triangle Dragon attacks you directly!

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:22.600
I win!

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:23.790
You fool!

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:26.640
I’ll show you.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:30.190
Cringe before Hanoi’s noble power!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.150
I activate my trap!

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:47.450
What?  This energy reading 
is different than before!

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.130
Is it a duel?

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:57.980
A dead end!

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:00.170
What are we gonna do?

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.020
We’re saved!

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:16.560
But what was that?

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:19.310
It's a different abnormality.

00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:22.800
Yeah.  That light is definitely dangerous.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:24.070
Let’s go.

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.290
I knew you'd do this!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.130
What's that?

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.420
That's where Ghost Girl went!

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:46.860
What's this?

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:51.630
That’s…

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:52.900
Revolver?

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.890
Why is Ghost Girl dueling him?

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:57.800
All my monsters are destroyed.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:02.900
But if he used his trap at the start, 
he wouldn’t have taken damage.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:10.610
Was it so that he could activate his Skill?

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:17.080
Since you didn't anticipate this, you’re 
a third-rate cyber treasure hunter.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.400
I can’t refute that.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.680
But I still have my pride!

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:25.280
I have to let people know what’s happening!

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:27.420
I’m the only one who can!

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:30.880
Primebanshee’s effect.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.880
When it's sent from the 
field to the graveyard...

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:37.900
...I can add one Altergeist 
in my graveyard to my hand!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:43.240
I return Altergeist Marionetter to my hand!

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:48.020
He lost LP so that he could use Storm Access.

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:50.480
But I won’t let him!

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:53.860
I activate the Skill, Secret Cure!

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:59.830
I flip over cards in my deck until I get a 
monster, and I add that monster to my hand.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:06.290
And we both gain LP equal 
to that monster’s ATK!

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:12.770
I see.  You’re trying to stop 
me from using Storm Access.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.350
The first card.

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:19.390
Kunquery has 0 ATK.

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:21.750
Therefore, you don’t regain LP.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:24.420
You’re third rate.

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:26.620
Luck has forsaken you.

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.260
I end my turn.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:31.520
It’s my turn!  I draw!

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:35.960
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Altergeist Protocol!

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:41.070
You can't negate the activation 
and effects of Altergeists!

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:44.370
And once per turn, I can negate 
your monster’s effect...

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:49.310
...by sending a different 
Altergeist to the graveyard!

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:55.320
Since I have Protocol and Kunquery, I can 
deal with effects and direct attacks.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:14:02.010
And if I resurrect Silquitous from my 
graveyard, I can return his card to his hand.

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:04.320
I'll at least survive this turn.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:08.060
Sorry, but I won’t let 
you activate that card.

00:14:08.060 --> 00:14:12.140
From my hand, I activate the 
Counter Trap, Red Reboot!

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:13.870
From your hand?

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:19.060
By paying half my LP, I can 
activate this card from my hand.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:22.840
It negates your trap card’s 
activation and effects...

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.080
...and sets it again.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:31.420
And if you have a trap card in 
your deck, I can also set that.

00:14:31.420 --> 00:14:38.030
Due to Red Reboot, you can’t 
activate trap cards this turn.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:46.100
I set one card.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:52.040
He needs 1000 or fewer LP to activate 
Storm Access, and I couldn't prevent that.

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:58.590
But I have the advantage 
in LP, hand and the field.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.080
I still have a chance!

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:05.360
You actually think you’re going to survive?

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:10.720
Only the darkness of death awaits you.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:14.360
Which you can’t escape from!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:19.200
I activate Background Dragon’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:20.670
From the graveyard?

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:24.940
When there are no monsters on my field...

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:28.460
...I can Special Summon this card 
and a Level 4  or lower Dragon

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:30.640
from my hand in defense position.

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:33.970
Resurrect, Background Dragon!

00:15:35.320 --> 00:15:37.950
And appear from my hand!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.790
Sniffer Dragon!

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:48.860
Sniffer Dragon’s effect activates 
when it's summoned or Special Summoned.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:55.070
I add another Sniffer Dragon from 
my deck to my hand and summon it!

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:01.780
I'll now show you my new power.

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:07.850
I can hear the pulse of an unknown 
power hiding in the network.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:15.370
It’s waiting for me to take it.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:20.090
Come, Data Storm!

00:16:22.730 --> 00:16:23.800
This is…

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.840
I activate my Skill!

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:41.930
The new breath resides in my hand!

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:48.050
Storm Access!

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:51.790
This power is good.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:17:00.000
Manifest!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:17:01.900 --> 00:17:03.760
Arrowheads confirmed.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:07.410
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Effect Monsters!

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:13.610
I set Background Dragon and two 
Sniffer Dragons in the Link Markers!

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.270
Circuit combine!

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:24.450
Appear, Link 3 Topologic Trisbaena!

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:34.010
A new Topologic!

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:39.210
Defrag Dragon’s effect 
activates from my graveyard.

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:45.810
I can Special Summon it by banishing three 
monsters with the same name from my graveyard.

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:49.890
I banish three Sniffer 
Dragons from my graveyard.

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:52.620
Resurrect, Defrag Dragon!

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.970
Trisbaena’s effect!

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:58.590
When a monster is Special 
Summoned next to its link...

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:04.100
...that monster and all our cards in our 
Spell & Trap Card Zones are banished.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:10.090
And for every one of your banished 
cards, you take 500 damage.

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:11.970
Migration Force!

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:15.240
Battle!

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:19.930
Topologic Trisbaena attacks 
Ghost Girl directly!

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:21.520
Vanish!

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:29.720
Final Vulnerable Code!

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:39.370
He played me in the palm of his hand.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:53.950
Hang in there, Ghost Girl!

00:18:56.340 --> 00:19:00.780
F-For a professional, I'm pathetic.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:03.380
Hold on!  I’ll save you!

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.260
This is more important.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:10.040
This treasure is incredible.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:13.370
The best I've ever acquired.

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:28.320
You must take that data out of here.

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:35.620
As you said, something is 
happening in LINK VRAINS.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:39.720
Okay.  I promise.

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:49.130
What’s happening?

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:52.140
Be careful of Revolver.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:56.010
He has a terrifying card-

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:57.740
Ghost Girl!

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:03.560
The way she vanished was horrible!

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:06.820
You’re late, Playmaker.

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:09.920
Revolver!  What did you do with Ghost Girl?

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:13.960
She became the foundation to save the world.

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:16.260
She won’t come back.

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:18.860
What are you doing?

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.870
The Tower of Hanoi has already activated.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:27.570
If you want to stop this game, 
you must defeat me, Playmaker.

00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:35.250
Revolver!

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:39.000
Wait, Revolver!

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:41.860
Hey, Playmaker!

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:45.540
You promised Ghost Girl that 
you'll bring back the data!

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:47.830
Come back, Revolver!

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:57.880
Playmaker, we're in real danger!

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:05.820
Log out!

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:11.080
LINK VRAINS is still at peace.

00:21:13.710 --> 00:21:15.060
What’s going on?

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:23.160
What what?

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:25.200
What what what?

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:32.140
What's happening?

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:34.340
Kusanagi!

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:35.530
Yusaku.

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.050
What’s that?

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:15.510
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:22.650
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:29.880
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:30.380 --> 00:22:37.230
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:44.470
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:44.850 --> 00:22:48.620
There were fragments of power

00:22:48.850 --> 00:22:55.800
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:56.030 --> 00:23:03.140
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:10.320
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:17.550
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:24.400
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:32.100
Lighting Life with our invisible bond

00:23:37.150 --> 00:23:41.630
The structure is too tall for a tower.

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:44.720
It absorbs everything, splitting the earth

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:48.260
and climbing through the 
clouds to the heavens.

00:23:48.910 --> 00:23:51.770
The unprecedented event now begins.

00:23:51.770 --> 00:23:55.260
The time limit to demise is six hours.

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:58.420
Is this the game Revolver talked about?

00:23:58.420 --> 00:24:02.120
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Tower of Hanoi

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.180
Into the VRAINS!
